A||||4||GREENDANO||I found out what's up with IRM||||1||
Z||000000||GREENDANO||01-11-2000||05:35 PM||||This is copied from V8 Archie's message board:  <P>I know that there were some questions about the status IRM on the<BR>"other" list the other day. I've  known  what was going on for a couple<BR>of months now but I didn't have express permission to pass it on until<BR>now.<P>I had a long conversation with Jim Sutter this AM, and I am assured that<BR>he is gradually getting better.  As some of you know, Jim has been<BR>"into" restoring Vintage Sprint Cars for the last 2 or 3 years.  He is<BR>really not "into" the Fiero stuff as much as he was prior to Sprint<BR>Cars.  However He and Barb have tried to continue to supply IRM parts to<BR>us Fiero owners.  And Barb has tried to keep the Electronics business<BR>(Jim's main business) going.<P>A few months ago, while messing around with the Sprint Cars, Jim had a<BR>Stroke.  One of his friends, who was there at the time, had the presence<BR>of mind to call 911 even as Jim protested.  Jim was saved and spent<BR>several weeks/months in the Hospital recovering enough that he could go<BR>home.<BR>Well he's finally home and doing the Physical Therapy thing to try to<BR>regain use of his left arm & leg.<P>His spirits are high and he is trying to keep up with business from the<BR>"Kitchen Table", however priority remains on full recovery & his main<BR>business.  Although<BR>Jim is not into the Internet thing, he did tell me to say "Hi" & he does<BR>send along his best wishes to past & future customers.<P>Some of the newer/younger Fiero owners may not know who Jim Sutter is<BR>but most everyone has heard of IRM.  I think it would be safe to say<BR>that Jim is one of the top 10 people who promoted the joy of Fiero<BR>ownership into the fame it now enjoys.<P>I've gone to, & displayed at,  the Carlisle Kit Car show every year<BR>since it started.  As far as I can remember, Jim & IRM have not put up a<BR>company display at Carlisle.  But Jim has attended the show every year<BR>as a spectator.  With great pride I can tell you that EVERY year Jim<BR>stops by my booth area "to just shoot the bull".  Some will say that I'm<BR>bragging & I guess I am.  It makes you beat on your chest when you think<BR>that someone like Jim thinks enough of you to stop by to visit every<BR>time he can.<P>It is my hope that at Carlisle once again this year, Jim will be there<BR>and stop by to say "Hi".  No matter what else happens THAT will make my<BR>Carlisle weekend a good one.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000001||GREENDANO||01-21-2000||08:04 PM||||This is an update.<BR>  I don't mean to speak unkindly about IRM, but if you need parts in a hurry, order from somewhere else.  I ordered brake hoses and a glovebox in early December and called them two weeks ago to inquire about the status of my order.  At that point I did not know about Jim having a stroke.  Having known that I would have left them alone so they could deal with their own problems.  Barbara said she would call me back later that day.  She did not.  I called back, two weeks later, (today), and talked to Barbara again.  My order was not shipped and she had no idea what was going on with it.  I cancelled my order.<BR>  My advice....  If you want to do business with IRM, as I have enjoyed doing so in the past, wait a while while so health problems get ironed out and they can return to the quality service they used to deliver in the past.  <BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000002||WGraffiKs||01-24-2000||07:46 PM||||I assume IRM does NOT have a web site?||||reg||5
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||01-24-2000||07:58 PM||||Closest I've seen is a website that had low-quality scans of catalog pages..<P>the only product of theirs that I really like (of the ones I've seen) are the sidescoops.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||01-24-2000||09:05 PM||||No, they don't have a website. Just an e-mail address. <BR>I've bought a stainless "muffler eliminator" exhaust system from IRM. Has Hooker resonator tips. Was decent quality, but louder'n hell. Ended up having a bullet glasspack welded in, upstream. Still loud enough to chirp the car alarms in our parking garage at work, but it has a nice rumble to it.||||reg||1
